Still the shopkeeper in a pit and me with two hp problem ...

I've thought of an additional solution.

1) Step out of line of fire and engrave "E" as before.
2) read cursed scroll of charging and charge wand of poly to get one,
count 'em , one charge in the wand.
3) Wait for the shopkeeper to step out of the pit and step next to me
-- if I play it right he won't be able to line up the WoS before
closing to melee range.

4) At this point,  I break the wand of polymorph.   The resulting
explosion will poly both him and myself.

This has a number of effects:
1) He will almost certainly poly into something that will respect
Elbereth, ensuring my safety.
2) There is a chance ... not a spectacular one, but a chance
nonetheless.. that he won't have hands. In which case he won't be able
to use the wand of striking to kill me.
3) *I* will poly.  There are a number of possibilities:

A) I will poly into a stronger monster.   In which case, I can escape
with hit points or even kill him.

B) I poly into a weaker monster. In which case, if he hits me I return
to full strength human form with all hit points.

The drawback, of course, is that I will certainly losed my cursed
leather armor and my cloak.  Too bad.   armor, especially leather
armor, is fairly common in the mines and I'm sure I can find something
better.


The other drawback is that he might poly into something like an
arch-lich and I would poly into a grid bug.  But that's only a chance.
I'm trading certain death for possible death. I'll make that trade any
day. 

